                 Files shipped: lib/pn-mesh-page-device.{c,h},
                 lib/pn-mesh-page-network.{c,h},
                 lib/pn-mesh-page-security.{c,h}; deltas in
                 lib/pn-mesh-connection.{c,h}, lib/pn-mesh-dialog.c,
                 lib/Makefile.am.

                 Gotchas for any future Config sub-block writer
                 (none yet planned; Phase 11/13 are postponed):

                 (i) BYTES round-trip via GBytes.  ipv4_config,
                 public_key, private_key are length-delimited
                 bytes sub-fields.  Stash them on PnMeshState as
                 GBytes* (own-on-parse, free-on-close, clear in
                 clear_state) and ref+copy into a per-call struct
                 in the async wrapper so the worker thread sees a
                 stable input even if the page rebuilds its ctx
                 mid-flight.

                 (ii) REPEATED bytes (admin_key).  Same recipe but
                 a GPtrArray-of-GBytes with g_bytes_unref as the
                 free func, allocated up front in open_sync and
                 set_size(0) at the top of each parse pass.  The
                 async wrapper deep-copies the array (g_bytes_ref
                 each entry) before handing it to the thread.

                 (iii) "I understand" check.  Reset to FALSE on
                 every set_state and after a successful Apply --
                 a sticky check would let a user accidentally
                 re-Apply a stale config after a handshake gave
                 fresh data.

Phase 8 (Plugin extraction) is no longer tracked under TODO #29 --
moved out 2026-05-28: it is its own cross-cutting project (Devices
menu becomes plugin-driven via a new PnDeviceProvider core API; the
meshtastic dialog code migrates into the meshtastic plugin's GUI
companion; PnMeshtastic nodes gain a "Set up device..." affordance
that pre-picks the device).  Will get its own TODO entry when picked
up.

Gotchas worth re-reading before each phase (from pip-mesh, costly to
rediscover): always drain stale bytes before any handshake; never
wait for an end marker, wait for silence (3s config, 5s metadata);
sleep 0.5 after every write; bare set_channel is no-reboot,
commit_edit_settings persists+may reboot -- transactional only when
needed; cache invalidation keyed on USB VID:PID (the tty name gets
reused); frame magic is 0x94 0xC3, length is 2-byte BIG-endian;
short-name <=4 chars, long-name <=39, PSK exactly 32 or 64 hex chars.
The pip-mesh --help string flags --list-messages as broken; trust
the help text not the man page.

Hard rules (do not inherit from pip-mesh): no ~/.cache/, no
auto-detect on dialog open, no "auto-select if exactly one device",
no --raw or --max-messages CLI modes leaking into the GUI, no global
HEXDATA/PB_POS state -- each PnMeshConnection holds its own.

(30) MQTT node hardening (from the 2026-05-28 code review of
lib/pn-mqtt.c/.h, lib/pn-mqtt-sink.c/.h, lib/pn-mqtt-profile.c/.h and
tests/unit/test-pn-mqtt*.c).  The nodes are sound and GTK-free; these
are the findings worth fixing.  NOTE: pn-mesh-page-mqtt.c is the
Meshtastic radio's MQTT-gateway page (#29), NOT one of these nodes.

  CRITICAL
  - C1  Sink reports every failure only via g_warning/g_message ->
        invisible from the desktop launcher (violates the "errors via
        failure message, not stdout" rule; cf. pn-http.c:272).  Offenders
        in pn-mqtt-sink.c: queued-publish fail :486, live publish fail
        :671, connect refused :564, invalid URL :731, mosquitto_new/
        connect_async/loop_start/username_pw_set/tls_set :744,766,774,
        782,795.  Emit success=FALSE + human-readable output instead.
        (Source has the same smell -- see L1.)
  - C2  restart_client() runs from _init() (pn-mqtt.c:1173,
        pn-mqtt-sink.c:1154), before construction/deserialization is done.
        Source: starts the network thread before a SUBCLASS (Sink,
        Tasmota, Zigbee2MQTT) has initialized its private state, yet
        on_mqtt_message calls klass->accept_topic() on the net thread.
        Sink: every credential setter (broker-profile/url/username/
        password/client-id, :854,859,875,880,885) re-runs restart_client,
        so loading a document fires ~5 full connect cycles in a burst.
        Fix: defer the initial connect to constructed()/g_idle and
        debounce reconnects into one idle instead of reconnecting
        synchronously in each setter.

  HIGH
  - H1  Network-thread read of priv->topic/priv->qos races runtime
        reconfigure (pn-mqtt.c:467-469).  The "no mutex for config fields"
        invariant assumes setters always stop_client (join the thread)
        first, but libmosquitto's AUTO-RECONNECT keeps the net thread
        alive and re-fires on_mqtt_connect with no stop_client -- so a
        reconnect can read priv->topic while a setter frees/replaces it
        (torn read / UAF).  Fix: snapshot topic/qos at connect time or
        guard with the existing lock.
  - H2  Stale-disconnect race during reconnect-while-restarting, present
        EQUALLY in both nodes.  The conn-state trampoline guards only on
        client != NULL (pn-mqtt.c:413, pn-mqtt-sink.c:514); neither has a
        real generation/epoch counter, so an old session's queued
        trampoline running after restart_client installs a new client can
        flip a live node back to red (and on the Source skip the genuine
        reconnect's re-subscribe).  Fix: capture a generation counter in
        the closure, compare in the trampoline.
  - H3  Sink drops buffered startup commands on flush failure:
        flush_pending (pn-mqtt-sink.c:476-492) pending_free's each entry
        unconditionally even when mosquitto_publish errored (:485),
        defeating the buffer-and-flush guarantee.  Fix: on NOMEM/CONN_LOST
        re-queue rather than discard.

  MEDIUM
  - M1  build_mqtt_message (pn-mqtt.c:592-598) mirrors only DOUBLE/INT64
        JSON scalars to data.value; a bare true/false payload sets nothing
        (breaks the 0.0/1.0 boolean convention), and int64 loses precision
        via get_double.  Add a JSON-boolean -> 0.0/1.0 case.
  - M2  Sink loses buffered messages on dispose (finalize :989) and on a
        runtime URL change keeps the backlog and flushes commands meant
        for broker A to broker B.  Decide + document; likely clear the
        queue when broker identity changes.
  - M3  Profile lacks TLS/CA-file, port-as-int, and keepalive fields.
        TLS is inferred from URL scheme only and mosquitto_tls_set(...NULL)
        uses the system trust store (pn-mqtt.c:771), so a PRIVATE-CA broker
        is unconfigurable; keepalive hard-coded to 60s.  Known/deferred.
  - M4  payload_len (gsize) cast to int at pn-mqtt-sink.c:483,666; >256MB
        hits MQTT's limit and mosquitto_publish rejects -- logged only to
        stderr (see C1).

  LOW / NIT
  - L1  Source: subscribe failure (pn-mqtt.c:469-475) g_warns then flips
        the node GREEN anyway -> looks healthy, receives nothing.
  - L2  Dead variable need_schedule (pn-mqtt.c:375,388,394).
  - L3  Default topic "#" + a primary broker profile = a freshly dropped
        node auto-subscribes to the entire broker (footgun, intentional).
  - L4  Empty-payload publish is dropped (pn-mqtt-sink.c:383) -> cannot
        clear a retained topic with a null payload; document in help.
  - N1  restart_client repeats the g_free(url/user/pass/cid/host) cleanup
        block ~5x per file; an out: goto would remove the divergence risk.
  - N2  Stale header docs: pn-mqtt.h says property "topic" but the
        installed name is "subscribe-topic" (:1101); pn-mqtt-sink.h omits
        broker-profile/topic-template.
  - N3  parse_mqtt_url is DUPLICATED across both .c files (divergence
        risk); a shared static + shared test would cover both.

  TEST COVERAGE -- DONE 2026-05-28.  The pure logic was extracted into a
  new GTK-free/mosquitto-free lib/pn-mqtt-util.{c,h} (both nodes now wrap
  it; this also de-dups parse_mqtt_url, closing N3) and covered by two new
  binaries -- tests/unit/test-pn-mqtt-profile.c and test-pn-mqtt-util.c.
  All five items landed:
  1. [x] Profile schema characterization (test-pn-mqtt-profile.c): 4 field
         names/kinds + password==PN_FIELD_SECRET + help page.
  2. [x] pn_mqtt_parse_url table: scheme->TLS+default-port (1883/8883),
         bare host:port, port-range and empty-host/leading-'/' rejection.
  3. [x] pn_mqtt_build_message data-bag contract: object->nested payload,
         number->value, text->coerced value, non-UTF-8->payload "",
         envelope qos/retained/success.  ALSO pins M1's current behaviour
         (JSON boolean does NOT set value) so a future M1 fix is a visible
         test change.
  4. [x] pn_mqtt_build_payload: template expansion, string + structured
         data.payload fallback, missing-payload drop.
  5. [x] Offline queue (pn_mqtt_pending_*): LEN-cap eviction, AGE discard
         with an INJECTED clock (now_us param) + FIFO order.  flush_pending's
         mosquitto_publish stays on the node; the policy is in util.
  test-pn-mqtt-util = 125 checks; full `make check` = 75/75.

  STILL OPEN: the review BUGS themselves (C1 errors-to-stderr, C2 init-time
  connect, H1 topic-read race, H2/H3 generation guard, M1 boolean->value).
  Priority order to tackle: C1, C2, H1, then H2/H3.  The tests above are a
  net for that work, not a fix for it.
